module

public import CFSG.Quasithin.MainConverse.ExceptionalSections.Reduction

/-!
# Proper simple sections in the exceptional converse

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, *The Classification of Quasithin Groups*,
Theorem 0.1.2, printed p.4, and the repeated Main Theorem on p.482.
The exceptional cases use the split-octonion G₂ groups, the actual derived
group G₂(2)′, the genuine D₄ graph-field triality groups, and Parrott's Tits
presentation. Model identifications must be multiplicative equivalences.

This module exposes the common reduction from all proper simple sections to
nonabelian simple sections of maximal subgroups. The family classifications
remain explicit premises of that reduction; no exceptional proper-K theorem
is asserted without discharging them. The final inclusion of its concrete
section list into the full known-simple catalogue is a separate input.
-/
